5. ALWAYS REFRESH LIVE DEPLOYMENT DATA WHEN ENTERING THE OVERVIEW
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Deployment Manager is a live operational module.

Whenever the user lands on the Deployment Manager Overview page, trigger the appropriate fresh namespace discovery.

This should happen when:

A. User opens Deployment Manager from another module.

B. User switches the selected application/namespace using the application switcher.

C. User leaves Overview and returns from Audit.

D. User leaves Overview and returns from RBAC.

E. User navigates to another module/sub-module and returns to Deployment Manager.

F. User switches back to Deployment Manager after being away from it.

The intent is:

ENTER OVERVIEW
        ↓
Start fresh discovery
        ↓
Show blue discovery spinner
        ↓
Discovery completes
        ↓
Render latest deployment state
        ↓
Play normal entrance animation

Do not unnecessarily refetch multiple times because of React re-renders.

There should be exactly one intentional discovery operation per relevant Overview entry/context change.

Avoid race conditions when:
- application changes quickly
- user switches tabs quickly
- component mounts/unmounts
- multiple effects execute during development mode
- previous discovery is still in progress

Cancel/ignore stale discovery results where appropriate so an older request cannot overwrite the newly selected namespace/application.

